From 42ffdaaeae7ee51e7db5d53d2b63713b63cd5133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:30:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: fix the structured data, publish the agent API, make
 IndexNow fire
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A deep audit of the machine-readable surface found seven real gaps. The
checklist items were done — llms.txt generated from live data, a connected @id
graph, 358 sitemapped URLs, QAPage/DefinedTermSet/HowTo where they belong. The
gaps were the things nobody looks at twice.

THE LIABILITY

aggregateRating was ratingValue "4.9" with reviewCount computed as
`testimonials.length * 18`. Neither number had a source, and it shipped on all
358 pages. Google's penalty for uncorroborated review markup is not losing the
stars — it is a manual action that strips every rich result from the domain,
including the HowTo, the FAQ, the QAPage and the AggregateOffer on 224 city
pages. Fabricating one number risked all of it.

Removed. `company.reviews` is null and `reviewsLd()` emits nothing while it
stays that way, with the honest path back written into data/company.ts. The
testimonials still render as copy; they are simply no longer asserted to a
search engine as verified review data.

BROKEN OR DANGLING

  - The sitelinks SearchAction pointed at /guides/{search_term_string}.
    /guides/[slug] sets dynamicParams=false, so every expansion was a 404. It
    now points at /search?q=, and a test asserts the target is a real route.
  - 28 answer pages built an @id from company.website instead of SITE_URL.
    Until the domain cuts over those differ, so the QAPage author pointed at a
    node absent from the deployed graph. Same bug in /api/ask's grounding URL.
  - Structured pricing existed on the 224 long-tail pages and on none of the 8
    canonical service pages — the ones most likely to be cited when an
    assistant compares contractors.
  - /for-agents, the one page built for machines, was the only content page
    with no structured data on it.

A BUG I INTRODUCED AND THE TEST THAT NOW CATCHES IT

The first price parser took the first two dollar figures in the string. On
"From $650 minimum · $18–$35 / sq ft affected" that produced lowPrice 650 and
highPrice 18 — a high below its low, published to the JSON API and emitted as
an invalid AggregateOffer. parsePriceBand() now matches the range pattern
itself and returns null rather than inventing a ceiling for "Quoted per
project". tests/agent-api.test.ts asserts low < high for every band emitted.

DATES THAT WERE NOT DATES

`guide.updated` sat on the page, unused, while three surfaces each invented
their own answer: the sitemap stamped new Date() on all 358 URLs (so every
deploy claimed all 358 pages changed at once), the Article node carried the
string "2026-08-27" on all 19 guides, and the RSS feed had no date at all —
pubDate being the one field an aggregator uses to detect new content.
updatedDate() derives from what the page already tells a reader, and a test
fails on any hardcoded date string.

THE DIFFERENTIATOR THAT WAS HIDDEN

/api/ask had no CORS headers and no OPTIONS handler, so no browser-based agent
could call it, and it was documented only in a repo file no machine reads.

  - CORS and preflight on every agent endpoint
  - /api/facts.json    entity card, areas, stair-code thresholds, diagnostics
  - /api/services.json services with numeric price bands and units
  - /api/areas.json    32 areas with travel tiers and per-city URLs
  - /.well-known/agents.json  one directory of all of the above
  - all four published in llms.txt and ai.txt, where machines actually look

INDEXNOW, BUILT AND NEVER FIRED

No key file was committed, nothing called it, and its URL list was a second
hand-maintained copy of the sitemap that omitted /problems, /methods, /answers
and /glossary. It now derives from the built sitemap, refuses to announce a
vercel.app host, exits 0 when unconfigured, and runs from a workflow after CI
passes on main.

Also: robots.txt keeps naming only real sitemaps — listing llms.txt there
would advertise it in one line and produce a standing "could not be read"
error in Search Console. LocalBusiness gains contactPoint, paymentAccepted,
currenciesAccepted and an additionalType pointing at Wikidata, and sameAs moved
to data/company.ts with instructions for adding profiles as they are claimed.

147 tests. 358 pages, 358 unique titles, 2,005 JSON-LD blocks, audit clean.
